From: Nikolay Pisarev <nipisarev@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:09:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Cromarc H14: the space theme is the window's background

Zen draws the space theme, its gradient and grain, under the whole window,
and the toolbar and the space round the page stay clear over it. In Cromarc
windows (normal ones, with the sidebar) the frame view paints the theme
through cromarc::PaintWindowBackground, over the window material or the
frame colour; once Chrome has made the window non-opaque for its glass
frame, Cromarc puts Zen's window material under it instead of Chrome's
glass, tint and opaque backing; MultiContentsBackgroundView leaves its area
clear; and CustomCornersBackground (toolbar, top container, tab strip
region) lets Cromarc paint instead: nothing, but Zen's compact toolbar
background for the sidebar floating over the page.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_frame_view_mac.mm b/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_frame_view_mac.mm
index 8354a9179ef79..cc472581d82bb 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_frame_view_mac.mm
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_frame_view_mac.mm
@@ -66,6 +66,7 @@
 #include "ui/views/controls/label.h"
 #include "ui/views/layout/layout_types.h"
 #include "ui/views/widget/widget.h"
+#include "cromarc/hooks/hooks.h"  // Cromarc
 
 namespace {
 
@@ -502,6 +503,9 @@ void BrowserFrameViewMac::OnPaint(gfx::Canvas* canvas) {
   if (is_glass_frame_eligible_) {
     // In glass mode, painting to frame color happens in the opaque background
     // view instead.
+    // Cromarc: the space theme over the glass.
+    cromarc::hooks::PaintWindowBackground(canvas, GetLocalBounds(),
+                                          GetBrowserView());
     return;
   }
 
@@ -514,6 +518,9 @@ void BrowserFrameViewMac::OnPaint(gfx::Canvas* canvas) {
   if (!theme_service->UsingSystemTheme()) {
     PaintThemedFrame(canvas);
   }
+  // Cromarc: the space theme over the frame colour.
+  cromarc::hooks::PaintWindowBackground(canvas, GetLocalBounds(),
+                                        GetBrowserView());
 }
 
 void BrowserFrameViewMac::Layout(PassKey) {
diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_native_widget_mac.mm b/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_native_widget_mac.mm
